# STAGED REJECT (owner ruling, decisions.md 2026-07-16 STAGING RULING): a field
# access on a `Box[P]` (`b.x`) requires §9.4 deref coercion, which is
# UNIMPLEMENTED end-to-end (the auto-deref field READ yields garbage 0 at
# runtime; method auto-deref fails to compile). The earlier `check_gg_ok`
# staging blessed that silent wrong output — the Core-#8 red-flag pattern — so
# acceptance is REVERSED: `gg check` must FAIL with
# `error[E_DerefCoercionUnimplemented]` ("field `x` exists on `P` but deref
# coercion (design-doc §9.4) is not yet implemented for `Box`"). The field
# EXISTS on the inner type, so `E_NoFieldFound` would lie — the dedicated code
# names the real gap.
#
# When the deref-coercion BACKEND track lands (TODO.md "RV-A scout discoveries"
# items 1+2, the Strategy-2B deref-field-read work), it flips this back to
# acceptance AND un-ignores the runtime twin (`fieldaccess_box_field_read_value`)
# asserting the CORRECT value `7` — per "Don't redesign around compiler gaps",
# the expected runtime output stays the right one, never the buggy one.
from std.collections import Box

struct P:
    int x

int main():
    Box[P] b = Box.new(P(7))
    print(b.x)
    return 0
